+/*
+ * ASK2 OH-port re-enqueue infra (dpaa1), phase 1c/1d de-risk tool:
+ * /sys/kernel/debug/fman_port_oh_test/bringup -- hand-arm the ONE call that
+ * exercises phase 1b's dormant code (init_bmi_oh()/set_oh_dflt_cfg()/the
+ * fman_set_port_params() mac_mfl fix) on real silicon for the first time,
+ * decomposed as its own smallest-possible step: fman_port_config()+
+ * fman_port_init() only. FMBM_OCFG[EN] is NOT touched here (stays 0, see
+ * fman_port_oh_enable()) -- a misconfigured-but-disabled port's registers
+ * take no effect, so this step alone is provably as safe as writing static
+ * config to a private per-port page can be, before anything is armed.
+ *
+ * Self-contained in this module rather than routed through fman_pcd.c's
+ * existing per-FMan debugfs tree (cc_test etc.): deliberate choice after
+ * finding this project's own local kernel-source build cache had drifted
+ * into an inconsistent state for those files (unrelated to O/H work) --
+ * a top-level debugfs node here has zero dependency on that tree's exact
+ * current shape.
